style='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f5f3ed;color:#232c28;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1080px;margin:auto;padding:32px 22px 70px}h1{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,48px);line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:42px;line-height:1.3}h3{font-size:23px;line-height:1.35;margin:8px 0}a{color:#245b46}nav{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap}nav a{min-height:44px;padding:8px 0}p,li,td,code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.table{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:650px}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd0c8}th{background:#e8ece4}article{border-top:2px solid #52685b;padding:20px 0 28px;scroll-margin-top:20px}.tag{font-size:14px;color:#58685d;margin:0}.proof{background:#e8ece4;padding:14px 18px;border-left:3px solid #6b856e}.proof p{margin:5px 0}details{padding:6px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px}select,input{font:inherit;padding:10px;min-height:44px;max-width:100%}.filters{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;align-items:center;margin:20px 0}button{font:inherit;min-height:44px;cursor:pointer}pre{overflow:auto;background:#e8ece4;padding:15px}li{margin:8px 0}[hidden]{display:none!important}.gridwrap{overflow-x:auto}.handgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(13,1fr);min-width:650px;gap:3px;margin:12px 0}.cell{min-height:40px;text-align:center;padding:5px;font-size:13px;background:#e1e3de}.cell.open{background:#c2d7c4}.cell.raise{background:#ecc5bf}.cell.call{background:#eee0b0}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #386c51;outline-offset:2px}'''
page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><link rel="icon" href="data:,"><title>Glass Table numerical audit — build 20</title><style>{style}</style></head><body><main><p>Glass Table · 2026-10-11 · Installed baseline 1.0(20)</p><h1>Are the app’s numbers correct?</h1><p>{summary}</p><p><strong>한국어 요약</strong> 족보 빈도와 핵심 계산은 독립 검증 결과와 일치했어요. 다만 본전인 EV를 손해로 설명하는 문구, PFR의 분모, 무승부 지분을 승률로 부르는 표현, 아웃 문제의 시작 상황과 무승부 설명에는 수정이 필요해요. 아래 수정안은 제안이며, 현재 설치된 앱에는 아직 반영하지 않았어요.</p><nav><a href="#verified">Verified values</a><a href="#charts">Every chart</a><a href="#findings">Corrections</a><a href="#scope">Coverage</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a></nav><h2 id="verified">Exact final-hand frequencies</h2><p>Best five from seven random cards, denominator 133,784,560. These are mutually exclusive best-hand categories. A flush is <strong>3.025494%</strong>, displayed as 3.0%. This is neither the chance of winning nor a conditional flush-draw probability. For a random five-card hand, a flush is 0.196540%; using that value for this seven-card lesson would be wrong.</p><div class="table"><table><tr><th>Category</th><th>Exact count</th><th>Exact count ÷ total</th></tr>{frequency}</table></div><p>The counts agree with independent enumeration and <a href="https://web.math.princeton.edu/~nalon/PDFS/skill4.pdf">Noga Alon’s exact table</a>. Separately rounded displayed percentages need not sum to exactly 100%. Royal and non-royal straight flushes are split here, so no category is counted twice.</p><h2 id="charts">Chart numbers and all hand memberships</h2><p>These charts are the app’s published Chen-based teaching model. Their arithmetic and action consistency can be verified; they cannot be certified as universally optimal poker strategy. Position, stacks, opponents, game structure and rake can change real strategy. One 169-cell chart is not169 equally likely deals: each pair cell has 6 combos, suited 4 and offsuit 12.</p><div class="table"><table><tr><th>Opening seat</th><th>Nominal RFI target</th><th>Opening combos</th><th>Actual RFI width</th><th>Classes</th><th>Defend: raise combos</th><th>Call combos</th><th>Fold combos</th></tr>{chartrows}</table></div><p>Defend columns divide all 1,326 starting combinations. Raise and call are disjoint; folds complete the partition. Nominal raise band is 30% of the opener’s nominal width; continue band 75%. The call-only band is their difference, not 75% on top of the raise band. Hero’s seat is intentionally ignored in this teaching model.</p><label>Opening seat <select id="seat">{''.join(f'<option>{e(r["seat"])}</option>' for r in charts)}</select></label><label>Chart <select id="chartmode"><option value="rfi">Open first / RFI</option><option value="defend">Respond to raise / Defend</option></select></label><p id="gridnote"></p><div class="gridwrap"><div id="grid" class="handgrid" aria-label="RFI opening membership, all169 classes"></div></div><p>In RFI, green cells open and other cells fold. In Defend, red means raise again, amber means call, and gray means fold. This is an audited data visualization, not a new app UI or strategy proposal. <a href="evidence/math/chart-membership.json">Full machine-readable action mapping</a> includes every defend action too. BB is absent from RFI because winning the blinds without an entrant ends the hand; its empty RFI and fold-only placeholder are separately exported, not taught as a decision.</p><h3>Opponent range targets and actual authored widths</h3><p>These are seven-seat averages of authored selection ranges, not observed action frequencies. Practice bots use headline widths without the graded table’s seat factors; casual bots also have stochastic choices.</p><div class="table"><table><tr><th>Style</th><th>VPIP target</th><th>Actual mean play width</th><th>PFR target</th><th>Actual mean raise width</th></tr>{archetyperows}</table></div><p><a href="evidence/math/archetype-counts-6x7.csv">All 42 style/seat rows</a> · <a href="evidence/math/chart-mapping-169x8.csv">All 169×8 hand/seat chart cells as CSV</a></p><h2 id="findings">Current issues and suggested corrections</h2><p>All recommendations preserve correct calculations and existing learning/progress definitions. Changes to a strategy model need separate design and regression review.</p><div class="filters"><label>Show <select id="kind"><option>All</option><option>Correct teaching</option><option>Correct display</option><option>Qualify</option></select></label><label>Find <input id="find" type="search" placeholder="e.g. equity, Korean, streak"></label></div><p id="shown"></p>{articles}<h2>Future-model risks, separate from current defects</h2><p><strong>Mixed range weights:</strong> range percentages support partial weights, but combo expansion drops those weights and equity/distribution APIs then treat expanded combos equally. A test range with AA weight 1 and 22 weight 0.01 incorrectly evaluates like equal-weight AA+22 in those APIs. Current published generated teaching ranges are pure0/1, so this is a future API risk, not evidence that current chart grades are wrong.</p><p><strong>Bet facing a raise:</strong> one graded EV branch averages the best continuation separately for each hidden opponent combo. That would give the player information they do not have. Independent source review found the branch unreachable under all current published policies: checked-to hands exclude betting buckets and raising buckets are subsets of betting buckets. Preserve that invariant; before expanding policies, maximize against the aggregate observed raising range.</p><h2>Interpretation checks to keep</h2><p>One-card outs approximation is not two-card probability. With 9 fixed outs and 47 unseen cards, the next-card chance is 19.1489% and the chance to encounter an out across two cards is 34.9676%. In this app’s face-up-opponent turn drill, 44 rivers remain:9/44=20.4545% outright wins. A rule-of-2 estimate gives 18%, already labeled approximate. Include tie shares separately for equity. These numbers assume the stated fixed-out/card set and do not guarantee a final win after an opponent redraw.</p><p>Call pricing uses the pot after the opponent’s bet and before your call. For pot 20, bet 10, call 10, the final pot is 40 and break-even equity 25%. MDF instead uses the pot before the bet:20/(20+10)=66.6667% defense against a zero-showdown-value pure bluff in the one-bet model. A correct MDF number is not an instruction to call every hand or a replacement for the chart.</p><p>Progress reports practice evidence, not certified poker skill. Help remains the learner’s choice and stays included in approved aggregate practice totals. Style intervals describe recent play against these bots; the repeated observations are not guaranteed independent. A 90% calibration target is the stated interval coverage target, not proof that the app teaches 90% of material or that a user remembers 90%.</p><h2 id="scope">Audit coverage and limits</h2><div class="table"><table><tr><th>Area</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Evidence / assumptions</th></tr>{coverrows}</table></div><p>Scanned 128 Swift source files and 6,087 numeric/probability-related source lines, including layout/constants and comments as discovery input. These are scan counts, not 6,087 verified learner claims. Current routed lessons, guides, advanced topics, graded 1v1, FreePlay, charts, Records and numeric feedback were traced by source. Existing tests and independent probes cover finite conditions; there is no blanket proof of every possible future input or every rendered state.</p><p>Light/dark share the numeric model. This audit checks data and bilingual meaning, not a new screenshot/layout pass. The <a href="../../../.build/native-ux-b20/index.html">build 20 native visual report</a> documents the previous EN/KO light/dark/AX checks separately. No reinstall or phone-data access was performed for this audit. One numerical verification limit remains: the graded flop uses 200 samples per opponent combo, and this audit has not bounded that sampling noise against the 0.5bb/2bb grade thresholds. Before claiming every borderline grade is stable, compare representative and near-threshold table decisions against exact runouts or a larger-sample reference; retain the existing sampled/checkdown disclosure meanwhile.</p><h2 id="evidence">Reproducible evidence</h2><p>Source commit <code>07054d0366b88ce268ae237cc26ce73291ad8adc</code>. Engine Release 93 tests passed. Drills 401 XCTest plus 75 Swift Testing passed. The tests passed despite the teaching issues because existing tests mostly check arithmetic and model consistency; independent semantic review found what those assertions did not cover.</p><ul><li><a href="evidence/math/engine-release.log">Engine Release test log</a> · <a href="evidence/math/drills-debug.log">Drills test log</a></li><li><a href="evidence/math/independent-probe.jsonl">Independent probe results</a> · <a href="evidence/math/AuditRunner/Sources/AuditRunner/main.swift">Independent best-five evaluator and probe source</a></li><li><a href="evidence/math/frequency7.json">Full independent seven-card census</a> · <a href="evidence/math/frequency7.cpp">Direct rank/suit census source</a></li><li><a href="evidence/root/source-inventory.json">Source hashes and raw numeric discovery inventory</a> · <a href="evidence/root/independent-combinatorics.json">Independent arithmetic</a> · <a href="evidence/root/semantic-counterexamples.json">Teaching counterexamples</a></li><li><a href="findings.json">Structured findings</a> · <a href="../../research/2026-10-11-poker-numbers-primary-sources.md">Primary-source research</a> · <a href="../../research/2026-10-11-numerical-math-audit.md">Detailed math audit</a></li></ul><p>Primary sources: <a href="https://ctools.ece.utah.edu/Probability/Combinatorics/ProbCombEx15.pdf">Utah combinatorial hand derivations</a>; <a href="https://web.math.princeton.edu/~nalon/PDFS/skill4.pdf">Alon’s poker mathematics</a>; <a href="https://web.fe.up.pt/~niadr/PUBLICATIONS/2013/TeofiloReisLopesCardoso_ComputingCardProbabilitiesInTexasHoldem.pdf">academic Chen reproduction</a> (not the original book); <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-spaced-repetition/py-fsrs/main/fsrs/scheduler.py">official FSRS reference</a> (defaults rechecked this audit).</p><h2>Recommended next correction pass</h2><p>FixN01–N07 first with generated counterexamples and date-controlled regressions, then refineN08–N12. Preserve chart policy, deterministic seeds, help-neutral summaries and saved data. Add tests that validate the explanation against the actual current hand, final win/tie/loss and exact due time, rather than only comparing values produced by the same implementation. Review any score/policy change separately.</p></main><script>const charts={json.dumps(charts)};const mappings={json.dumps(mapping,ensure_ascii=False)};const ranks=['A','K','Q','J','T','9','8','7','6','5','4','3','2'];function grid(){{let r=charts.find(r=>r.seat===document.querySelector('#seat').value);document.querySelector('#gridnote').textContent=r.seat+': '+r.combos+' combinations / 1326 = '+r.actualPercent.toFixed(4)+'%';let g=document.querySelector('#grid');g.replaceChildren();ranks.forEach((a,i)=>ranks.forEach((b,j)=>{{let hand=i===j?a+b:(i<j?a+b+'s':b+a+'o');let c=document.createElement('div');let mode=document.querySelector('#chartmode').value;let value=mode==='rfi'?(r.hands.includes(hand)?'open':'fold'):mappings.find(x=>x.hand===hand).seats[r.seat].defend;let role=value==='3벳'?'raise':value==='콜'?'call':value;let text=value==='3벳'?'raise again':value==='콜'?'call':value==='폴드'?'fold':value;c.className='cell '+role;c.textContent=hand;c.title=text;c.setAttribute('aria-label',hand+': '+text);g.append(c)}}))}}function filter(){{let k=document.querySelector('#kind').value;let q=document.querySelector('#find').value.toLowerCase();let n=0;document.querySelectorAll('article[data-kind]').forEach(a=>{{a.hidden=!(k==='All'||a.dataset.kind===k)||!a.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q);if(!a.hidden)n++}});document.querySelector('#shown').textContent=n+' findings shown'}}document.querySelector('#seat').addEventListener('change',grid);document.querySelector('#chartmode').addEventListener('change',grid);document.querySelector('#kind').addEventListener('change',filter);document.querySelector('#find').addEventListener('input',filter);grid();filter();</script></body></html>'''
